<title>PHILIPPINES: Piltel surges 6.06 pct in early trade.</title>
<headline>Piltel surges 6.06 pct in early trade.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cellular phone firm Pilipino Telephone Corp rose 60 centavos, or 6.06 percent, to 10.50 pesos in early Wednesday trade as investors bought the company's shares ahead of second half results.</p>
<p>&quot;People are positioning for the next six months, taking advantage of the current low valuation of the stock. They expect the anti-cloning measures to improve its system,&quot; said Henry Ong, an analyst at Sapphire Securities.</p>
</text>
